{Possible variation from Jussupow, Artur - Carlsen, Magnus, NH Chess Tournament 2006} 30... Qf3 {[%emt 0:00:01] threatens mate in one.} (30... Qh3 $4 {Also threatens mate in one. Exercise: Why does this lose?} 31. Qf6+ Rg7 32. Qxg7+ $1 {Elimination of the defender.} Kxg7 33. gxh3 $18) 31. g3 (31. Qxf7 Qxg2#) 31...
Rxg3+ $1 32. fxg3 Qxg3+ {Exercise: Calculate the continuation up to the forced mate.} 33. Kf1 (33. Kh1 Qh3+ (33... Qxe1+ {If you do not see the mate, this also wins.} 34. Kh2 Qf2+ (34... Rg8 $4 35. Qf6+ Rg7 36. Rc8#)
35. Kh3 Rg8 {[%csl Yf6][%cal Gf2f6] it is important that Black does not allow Qf6+
} 36. Rc3 (36. Rc8 Qg3#) 36... Qg2+ 37. Kh4 Qg4#) 34. Kg1 Rg8+ 35. Kf2 Rg2+ 36.
Kf1 Qh1# {Another file mate.}) 33... Qf3+ 34. Kg1 Rg8+ 35. Kh2 Qg2# (35... Qxh5+
{Also leads to mate.} 36. Qh4 Qxh4#) *

