1... Qh3 (1... Qe6 {[%cal Ge6e1] Black can threaten a back-rank mate in return} 2. h4 {But White can create an escape square for the king.} (2. Rb1 {This also prevents mate, but it cuts off the queen's path to f1.} Qh3 {
[%cal Rh3g2]})) 2. Qf1 {The only defensive move.} Qxf1+ (2... Re1 $5 {Also leads to mate. White deflects the white queen.} 3. Qxe1 Qg2#) (2... Rc1 $4 {But this does not help.} 3. Rb8+ Re8 4. Rxe8#) 3. Kxf1 Rc1# {Back-rank mate.} *

