17... Rxf3 $1 {You should sacrifice only when you are sure that it works. Here, it does.} 18. gxf3 (18. exd5 $5 {But this also has to be calculated.} Rf4 $5 $19 {Traps the queen and is immediately clear.} (18... Rxd5 19.
Rxd5 (19. gxf3 Qg5+ 20. Kh1 Bh3 21. Rg1 Rxd1) 19... Bxd5 20. gxf3 Qg5+ 21. Qg4
(21. Kh1 Bxf3#) 21... Qxg4+ 22. fxg4 Bxb3 23. Rb1 Na5 $1 $17 {Black has a material advantage in the endgame.})) 18... Bh3 19. Kh1 {Defends against mate.} (
19. Rfe1 Qg5+ 20. Kh1 Qg2#) 19... Qf7 $1 {Black insists on delivering mate.}
20. Nd2 (20. Rd3 Bxf1 $19) 20... dxe4 21. Qxe4 (21. fxe4 Rxd2 $1 22. Rxd2 Qf3+
23. Kg1 Qg2#) 21... Bxf1 $19 {White cannot take the bishop.} 22. Rxf1 (22.
Nxf1 Rxd1) 22... Rxd2 *

